30,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The physical situation is problematic. Some spots are exposed to rain, and the congestion in the mornings is causing people to shift other bikes just to leave. We need a solution that addresses this chaos.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Financially, we have very little in the shared account for any major upgrades. Also, the nearby ward park is expensive and has a long waiting list, so we can't simply rely on external options.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,George,,"It seems the same people have held the best spots for years without any review. Interestingly, those who use their bikes daily mentioned they would be willing to pay for a space.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's a mess. Complaints about leaning bikes just vanish because there's no accountability. Also, a neighbor's attempt at charging for spaces caused arrears and social isolation. We should be careful not to kill the community spirit.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I'm worried about the workload! The treasurer already spends hours on small collections, and adding more billing would be a lot. Also, those fancy display frames look tricky to use and need regular maintenance. We can't just add more work!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, if the display frames are high-maintenance and difficult, we should avoid them. @George, since daily users are willing to pay, perhaps a financial incentive could solve the congestion I observed.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, a fee might work, but we must consider the impact. @Shunichi mentioned that charging caused social friction nearby. We need a balance between fairness and maintaining a good atmosphere in the building.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,George,,"I agree with Ryuji. While some are willing to pay, we must be cautious. However, the fact that the same flats have held the best spots for five years without review is a problem that needs fixing.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. The current ""invisible"" rules are just as damaging as a bad new one. If we don't change something, the resentment George mentioned will only grow, even if people are too polite to complain.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Mio,,"But if we make it too complicated, who's going to do the work? I don't want us to pick a plan that just burns out one person. We need something simple that doesn't add more paperwork!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, simplicity is key. If we avoid complex billing or high-maintenance equipment, we reduce the burden. @George, since the current allocation is stagnant and unfair, we must move toward a system that rotates or justifies the spots.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"If we want to avoid the social friction Shunichi mentioned and the administrative burden Mio is worried about, we should look for a method that is transparent and requires minimal ongoing management.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,George,,"I agree. A transparent system would stop the grumbling about favoritism. If we can find a way to rotate the spaces or allocate them fairly without creating a mountain of paperwork, that would be the ideal path.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's be realistic. If we go for a system that's too rigid or creates financial winners and losers, we're just trading one kind of resentment for another. We need a solution that's clean and final.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I agree! Let's make sure whatever we choose doesn't turn into a second job for someone. If it's easy to set up and doesn't need constant checking, everyone will be much happier!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We have established that the current state is physically chaotic and socially stagnant. We need a system that is low-maintenance for Mio, financially neutral for Ryuji, and transparent for George and Shunichi.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Ryuji"",""George"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. We need a solution that doesn't require a large initial investment from our limited funds, nor one that creates a permanent administrative burden or deep social divides. Let's see which options fit these criteria.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,George,,I believe we are all in agreement on the requirements. We need to move away from the current stagnant arrangement while ensuring the new system is sustainable and doesn't damage our community. I look forward to the options.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's just hope the options aren't as dysfunctional as the current situation. As long as we don't pick something that turns the lobby into a battlefield, I'm satisfied. I'm ready to see what's on the table.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Mio,,I'm ready too! Let's hope for something super simple that doesn't make anyone's life a headache. I'll be voting for the easiest one to manage!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
