55,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option B is out; Mio found the double-tier racks difficult and high-maintenance. Option A risks the social friction Shunichi warned about. Option C is the most logical, fair, and low-maintenance choice.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, I agree. Option A's billing would burden the treasurer and potentially cause the social isolation Shunichi mentioned. Option C is financially neutral and requires very little ongoing administration.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,George,,"Option C solves the problem of the same flats holding the best spots indefinitely. It is transparent and fair, which should stop the grumbling without creating the financial divides that Option A might cause.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option C is the cleanest break. It avoids the ""pay-to-play"" resentment of A and the physical nightmare of B. A yearly draw is a simple ritual that keeps things fair without turning us into debt collectors.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option C sounds perfect! It's way easier than doing monthly billing, and we don't have to grease any springs. It's fair, simple, and won't make anyone's life a headache. I'm all for it!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"It seems we have reached a rare moment of total consensus. Option C addresses the physical congestion, the lack of transparency, and the administrative burden without risking the community's social harmony. I am ready to vote.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. Option C is the most cautious and reasonable approach given our limited budget and the risks of social friction. It provides a fair reset without creating a financial or administrative burden.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,George,,I am satisfied. It is a straightforward way to ensure no one is unfairly privileged and it requires very little effort to maintain. I will cast my vote for Option C.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,No need to overthink it. We've all agreed it's the least offensive and most practical choice. I'm voting for Option C.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Mio,,Me too! It's the simplest way to keep everyone happy and the paperwork low. I'm voting for Option C!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"Since we are all in agreement, I will cast my vote for Option C. It is the most rational solution to our current problems.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
